  "problem": "The average temperature in the Arctic in December of a particular year was ${3.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ Due to plummeting temperatures in the winter, the average temperature in February of the next year decreased by ${6.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to the average temperature in December. What was the average temperature in the Arctic in February?",
